 "capsule": "The Democratic Republic of the Congo gained independence from Belgium on 30 June 1960 under Prime Minister Patrice Lumumba and President Joseph Kasa-Vubu, but the state immediately fractured amid the Congo Crisis, Katanga's secession, and Lumumba's assassination in January 1961. Army commander Joseph Mobutu seized power in 1965, renaming the country Zaire in 1971 and ruling until rebel forces led by Laurent-Désiré Kabila overthrew him in 1997 and restored the name Democratic Republic of the Congo; Kabila's 2001 assassination brought his son Joseph Kabila to power amid the devastating Second Congo War (1998-2003), and Félix Tshisekedi has been president since 2019 amid continuing conflict with M23 rebels in the east.",
